From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: Update MTK BSS channel caches after channel changes

MTK ACS initially reports only the primary frequency. A later channel
notification supplies channel state for one BSS, although AP BSSs on
that radio share the operating channel. Updating only that BSS leaves
other BSS channel caches stale.

For device AP SME with MTK ACS support, nl80211 updates sibling BSS
frequency and bandwidth before reporting the completed switch.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211_event.c
@@ -1349,6 +1349,24 @@ static void mlme_event_ch_switch(struct
 			if (bw)
 				bss->flink->bandwidth = channel_width_to_int(
 					data.ch_switch.ch_width);
+#ifdef CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MTK
+			if (drv->mtk_do_acs && drv->device_ap_sme &&
+			    is_ap_interface(drv->nlmode) && !bss->valid_links) {
+				struct i802_bss *other;
+
+				/* MTK driver reports the radio channel on
+				 * one BSS; its other BSSs use the same channel. */
+				for (other = drv->first_bss; other;
+				     other = other->next) {
+					if (other == bss || other->valid_links)
+						continue;
+					other->flink->freq = bss->flink->freq;
+					if (bw)
+						other->flink->bandwidth =
+							bss->flink->bandwidth;
+				}
+			}
+#endif /* CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MTK */
 		}
 	}
 
